# Holmes scan exclusions.
#
# Holmes does not read .gitignore automatically, so this file must mirror
# every exclusion that already applies to the repository, plus the
# Holmes-specific additions below. If you add an entry to .gitignore that
# should also be excluded from security scans, add the matching pattern
# here too.

# --- Mirrors .gitignore ---
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/
.aws-sam/
frontend/dist/
frontend/dist-ssr/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local
frontend/.env.*.local
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
samconfig.toml
.coverage
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
/tmp/
kiro-cost-analyzer.zip
frontend/src/assets/
frontend/public/icons.svg
.hypothesis/
.threatmodel/
.repolinter/
.bedrock_agentcore/
.bedrock_agentcore.yaml
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.tmp-issues/
.holmes/
*.drawio.bkp
.$*.drawio.bkp

# --- Holmes-specific additions ---
# Generated by `make deploy-frontend` from live CloudFormation stack outputs
# for the deployer's own AWS account (API Gateway URL, Cognito IDs). Already
# covered by frontend/.env.production above via frontend/.env* patterns, but
# listed explicitly since it's the one that actually triggered this file.
frontend/.env.production

# Git metadata and CI-irrelevant local editor/build state not already covered.
.git/
build/
